{number: 106}
{title: Blest Be the Tie}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Blest be the [C7] tie that [F] binds
Our [Bb] hearts in [F] Christian [C7] love;
The [F] fellowship of [Bb] kindred [F] minds
Is [Bb] like to [F] that a-[C7] [F] bove.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Be-[F] fore our [C7] Father's [F] throne
We [Bb] pour our [F] ardent [C7] prayers;
Our [F] fears, our hopes, our [Bb] aims are [F] one,
Our [Bb] comforts [F] and our [C7] [F] cares.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
We [F] share our [C7] mutual [F] woes,
Our [Bb] mutual [F] burdens [C7] bear;
And [F] often for each [Bb] other [F] flows
The [Bb] sympa-[F] thizing [C7] [F] tear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
When [F] we a-[C7] sunder [F] part,
It [Bb] gives us [F] inward [C7] pain;
But [F] we shall still be [Bb] joined in [F] heart,
And [Bb] hope to [F] meet a-[C7] [F] gain.
{end_of_verse}
